  "prefLabel": "En 608.02 Resuscitation",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "En 608.02 Resuscitation.\n\n(a) Each water utility shall institute and maintain a program instructing its employees engaged in electrical work or work in hazardous atmospheres, such as in-ground pump stations or meter vaults, in safety procedures for resuscitation emergencies.\n\n(b) Copies of safety procedures shall be furnished to each such employee.\n\n(c) Electrical work as used herein shall be construed to mean work on all live electric conductors and equipment.\n\nSource. #13911, eff 3-21-24 (see Revision Note at chapter heading for En 600)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/en600.html"
